WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:07.930
Halloween traditions in America are linked to Celtic beliefs in ancient Britain.

2
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:21.130
The Celts believed that spirits of the dead would return to their homes on October 31, the day of the autumn feast.

3
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:31.090
Celts would build huge fires to frighten away any evil spirits that might return.

4
00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:41.190
People from Scotland and Ireland brought these ideas with them when they came to America.

5
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:50.770
Some believed that spirits played tricks on people on the last night of October.

6
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:58.090
In modern America, the holiday mostly belongs to children.

7
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:05.030
After dark, children wear special clothing, called costumes.

8
00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:14.290
They often appear as frightening creatures like vampires, ghosts and witches.

9
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:21.530
The children walk around their neighborhoods, knocking on doors of homes.

10
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:28.430
When someone answers a door, the children yell "trick or treat."

11
00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:38.710
If the people in the homes do not give them a sweet treat, the children may play a trick on them.

12
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:47.110
Some of the purchases people make for Halloween include candy and costumes.

13
00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:59.510
This year, the N.R.F. expects the superhero character Spider-Man to be the most popular children’s costume.

14
00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:07.310
Children are not the only Americans in costumes on Halloween, however.

15
00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:17.050
Adults also dress up in costumes and attend Halloween parties, parades and other events.

16
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:30.490
These celebrations often include costume competitions, with prizes for the most frightening, inventive or humorous costumes.

17
00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:46.130
Overall, the N.R.F. reports, total spending on costumes for Halloween 2024 is expected to reach a total of $3.8 billion.

18
00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:55.170
It says buyers will spend $3.5 billion on Halloween candy.
